{"4906610":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"Dead Market","steam_appid":4906610,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The market will lend you anything. It writes all of it down.<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dead Market is a card game about debt. You win a match by taking two of three rounds across three districts — but almost everything that wins a round is bought on credit, and the credit goes into a book that sits beside the board<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >for the whole match.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Ledger is the second board.<\/strong> Up to five lines, each with an amount in souls, a timer in turns, and sometimes Interest. Both players can read both books. The timer counts down at the start of your turn and nobody else's, and<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >when a line comes due you either pay it or default.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Defaulting is a move, not a mistake.<\/strong> Sometimes it is the correct one: against a small penalty it is often right to refuse, and against a large cost late in a round you are already losing, refusing is simply cheaper. The game is built around that decision being genuinely open. <\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>And the book has a floor under it.<\/strong> Take a sixth line while five are open and the line still goes in — but your oldest debt is called in that instant, whatever its timer said. A full Ledger is a loaded gun, and it is the most common way a new player loses a round they thought they had won.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Five factions, and each one uses the book differently<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Red Notaries<\/strong> — debt as a weapon. They put lines in your book and profit from them being there.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Grave Sovereigns<\/strong> — the Tomb is a resource. They kill their own units to trigger Last Wills, then buy them back. Killing their units is doing them a favour.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Candle Children<\/strong> — they Seal instead of killing, and they strike lines out of Ledgers. The only faction that reliably undoes debt.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Hungering Deep<\/strong> — they do not eat the dead. They eat that anything ever lived. Emptying your deck is a real win condition, and what they take is gone in a way the Tomb never is.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Free Mortals<\/strong> — numbers and refusal. Cheap bodies, wide boards, and cards that strike the opponent's book clean out of spite.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What is in it<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>247 playable objects<\/strong>, 190 of them collectible, every one with its ownillustration.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A six-act campaign<\/strong> with six bosses who each break one rule of thegame, and five endings that depend on clauses you initialled hours earlier.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Night Auction<\/strong> — a draft run. Lots come up, you take one card fromeach, and then you play the night out with a file the market lent you. Thehouse keeps a book on you while you do it.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Street of Unpaid Names<\/strong> — three standing contracts that neverexpire, and three more re-papered every day. No stamina. No waiting. Nothinghere is on a clock you have to come back for.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A ranked ladder<\/strong> of nine grades, and a card stall that opens on whatyou are missing rather than on what you have.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A first lesson that actually teaches<\/strong>: 53 steps over one scriptedmatch, dealt rather than shuffled, so every sentence it tells you is true twominutes later.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >It explains itself<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A player's guide of 26 sections that is generated against the rules themselves, so it cannot drift from them. A round end that reads itself out — every effect that fired, one at a time, ringed where it happened. And a line under the board<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >at all times answering &quot;why did that just happen?&quot;.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Accessibility<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Colour-vision profiles, high contrast, UI scaling, large card text, reduced motion, screen-shake and flashing toggles, subtitles, sound-effect captions, mono audio, a high-frequency reduction and a night mode. Seven separate volume<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >buses. Everything that carries meaning carries it in more than one channel.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >No account, no network, no telemetry<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It is a single-player game. It collects nothing and sends nothing anywhere.<\/p>","about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The market will lend you anything. It writes all of it down.<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dead Market is a card game about debt. You win a match by taking two of three rounds across three districts — but almost everything that wins a round is bought on credit, and the credit goes into a book that sits beside the board<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >for the whole match.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Ledger is the second board.<\/strong> Up to five lines, each with an amount in souls, a timer in turns, and sometimes Interest. Both players can read both books. The timer counts down at the start of your turn and nobody else's, and<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >when a line comes due you either pay it or default.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Defaulting is a move, not a mistake.<\/strong> Sometimes it is the correct one: against a small penalty it is often right to refuse, and against a large cost late in a round you are already losing, refusing is simply cheaper. The game is built around that decision being genuinely open. <\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>And the book has a floor under it.<\/strong> Take a sixth line while five are open and the line still goes in — but your oldest debt is called in that instant, whatever its timer said. A full Ledger is a loaded gun, and it is the most common way a new player loses a round they thought they had won.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Five factions, and each one uses the book differently<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Red Notaries<\/strong> — debt as a weapon. They put lines in your book and profit from them being there.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Grave Sovereigns<\/strong> — the Tomb is a resource. They kill their own units to trigger Last Wills, then buy them back. Killing their units is doing them a favour.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Candle Children<\/strong> — they Seal instead of killing, and they strike lines out of Ledgers. The only faction that reliably undoes debt.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Hungering Deep<\/strong> — they do not eat the dead. They eat that anything ever lived. Emptying your deck is a real win condition, and what they take is gone in a way the Tomb never is.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Free Mortals<\/strong> — numbers and refusal. Cheap bodies, wide boards, and cards that strike the opponent's book clean out of spite.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What is in it<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>247 playable objects<\/strong>, 190 of them collectible, every one with its ownillustration.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A six-act campaign<\/strong> with six bosses who each break one rule of thegame, and five endings that depend on clauses you initialled hours earlier.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Night Auction<\/strong> — a draft run. Lots come up, you take one card fromeach, and then you play the night out with a file the market lent you. Thehouse keeps a book on you while you do it.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Street of Unpaid Names<\/strong> — three standing contracts that neverexpire, and three more re-papered every day. No stamina. No waiting. Nothinghere is on a clock you have to come back for.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A ranked ladder<\/strong> of nine grades, and a card stall that opens on whatyou are missing rather than on what you have.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A first lesson that actually teaches<\/strong>: 53 steps over one scriptedmatch, dealt rather than shuffled, so every sentence it tells you is true twominutes later.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >It explains itself<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A player's guide of 26 sections that is generated against the rules themselves, so it cannot drift from them. A round end that reads itself out — every effect that fired, one at a time, ringed where it happened. And a line under the board<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >at all times answering &quot;why did that just happen?&quot;.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Accessibility<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Colour-vision profiles, high contrast, UI scaling, large card text, reduced motion, screen-shake and flashing toggles, subtitles, sound-effect captions, mono audio, a high-frequency reduction and a night mode. Seven separate volume<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >buses. Everything that carries meaning carries it in more than one channel.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >No account, no network, no telemetry<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It is a single-player game. It collects nothing and sends nothing anywhere.<\/p>","short_description":"A card game about debt. Win two of three rounds — but every advantage is bought on credit, and the Ledger beside the board is checked on every single turn. Five factions, 247 cards, and a market that will happily sell you something you cannot afford.","supported_languages":"English<strong>*<\/strong><br><strong>*<\/strong>languages with full audio support","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/b7a990cff1f1f20ce25c723c4e9b041c91a94b46\/header.jpg?t=1793645937","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/5314468363d1fa08c4491cba6a6caaa479b708f5\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793645937","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/5314468363d1fa08c4491cba6a6caaa479b708f5\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793645937","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> dual-core 2.0 GHz<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Vulkan 1.0 compatible GPU, 2 GB VRAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 2 GB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Sound Card:<\/strong> Any Windows-compatible device<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> Single-player and entirely offline. The game has no network code, no account and no telemetry; it never connects to anything.<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 11 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> quad-core 2.5 GHz<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 8 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Vulkan 1.0 compatible GPU, 4 GB VRAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 2 GB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Sound Card:<\/strong> Any Windows-compatible device<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> Single-player and entirely offline. The game has no network code, no account and no telemetry; it never connects to anything.<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"developers":["Bartjuh3"],"publishers":["Bartjuh3"],"price_overview":{"currency":"USD","initial":1199,"final":1019,"discount_percent":15,"initial_formatted":"$11.99","final_formatted":"$10.19"},"packages":[1703547],"package_groups":[{"name":"default","title":"Buy Dead Market","description":"","selection_text":"Select a purchase option","save_text":"","display_type":0,"is_recurring_subscription":"false","subs":[{"packageid":1703547,"percent_savings_text":"-15% ","percent_savings":0,"option_text":"Dead Market - <span class=\"discount_original_price\">$11.99<\/span> $10.19","option_description":"","can_get_free_license":"0","is_free_license":false,"price_in_cents_with_discount":1019}]}],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":false,"linux":false},"categories":[{"id":2,"description":"Single-player"},{"id":22,"description":"Steam Achievements"},{"id":64,"description":"Adjustable Text Size"},{"id":67,"description":"Camera Comfort"},{"id":66,"description":"Color Alternatives"},{"id":82,"description":"#category_contrast_controls"},{"id":68,"description":"Custom Volume Controls"},{"id":75,"description":"Keyboard Only Option"},{"id":76,"description":"Mouse Only Option"},{"id":80,"description":"#category_playable_at_your_own_pace"},{"id":74,"description":"Playable without Timed Input"},{"id":79,"description":"Save Anytime"},{"id":65,"description":"Subtitle Options"},{"id":23,"description":"Steam Cloud"},{"id":62,"description":"Family Sharing"}],"genres":[{"id":"23","description":"Indie"},{"id":"2","description":"Strategy"}],"screenshots":[{"id":0,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/9cd6f912c08d3f33ae9c99ff3cf676a6ec174f45\/ss_9cd6f912c08d3f33ae9c99ff3cf676a6ec174f45.600x338.jpg?t=1793645937","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/9cd6f912c08d3f33ae9c99ff3cf676a6ec174f45\/ss_9cd6f912c08d3f33ae9c99ff3cf676a6ec174f45.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793645937"},{"id":1,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/ada383cd75014cf11975cd5ead44803c5c53c23b\/ss_ada383cd75014cf11975cd5ead44803c5c53c23b.600x338.jpg?t=1793645937","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/ada383cd75014cf11975cd5ead44803c5c53c23b\/ss_ada383cd75014cf11975cd5ead44803c5c53c23b.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793645937"},{"id":2,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/6bb1c3a193d832355d61d429e84aeca7588d4877\/ss_6bb1c3a193d832355d61d429e84aeca7588d4877.600x338.jpg?t=1793645937","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/6bb1c3a193d832355d61d429e84aeca7588d4877\/ss_6bb1c3a193d832355d61d429e84aeca7588d4877.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793645937"},{"id":3,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/bfa97a44a19e6959f87e8640fd9bc9b8bda52e90\/ss_bfa97a44a19e6959f87e8640fd9bc9b8bda52e90.600x338.jpg?t=1793645937","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/bfa97a44a19e6959f87e8640fd9bc9b8bda52e90\/ss_bfa97a44a19e6959f87e8640fd9bc9b8bda52e90.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793645937"},{"id":4,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/8a95f99baffc015e46597302c3dadbe2074dcbeb\/ss_8a95f99baffc015e46597302c3dadbe2074dcbeb.600x338.jpg?t=1793645937","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/8a95f99baffc015e46597302c3dadbe2074dcbeb\/ss_8a95f99baffc015e46597302c3dadbe2074dcbeb.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793645937"},{"id":5,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/2f6284b84254d4b821d4c74d9dbdd47bd9a87ebb\/ss_2f6284b84254d4b821d4c74d9dbdd47bd9a87ebb.600x338.jpg?t=1793645937","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/2f6284b84254d4b821d4c74d9dbdd47bd9a87ebb\/ss_2f6284b84254d4b821d4c74d9dbdd47bd9a87ebb.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793645937"},{"id":6,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/06a6e9a7f9b739569fd1c528e9a8822366f3ce16\/ss_06a6e9a7f9b739569fd1c528e9a8822366f3ce16.600x338.jpg?t=1793645937","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/06a6e9a7f9b739569fd1c528e9a8822366f3ce16\/ss_06a6e9a7f9b739569fd1c528e9a8822366f3ce16.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793645937"},{"id":7,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/b89e8529869fbcd8193ed107d89a51a91c0cc5f8\/ss_b89e8529869fbcd8193ed107d89a51a91c0cc5f8.600x338.jpg?t=1793645937","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/b89e8529869fbcd8193ed107d89a51a91c0cc5f8\/ss_b89e8529869fbcd8193ed107d89a51a91c0cc5f8.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793645937"},{"id":8,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4906610\/d1748